  "data": {
    "body": "Consider a uniform rod of mass, \\textbf{M} = 4 \\textbf{kg} and length \\textbf{L} = 1.6 \\textbf{m} as shown. The rod is pivoted at point \\textbf{A} at the left end of the rod. Force of magnitude $\\mathbf{F_1}$ = 50 \\textbf{N} acts at the right end of the rod and the direction of the force makes $\\mathbf{\\theta_1}$ = $15^\\circ$ with the rod as shown. Force of magnitude $\\mathbf{F_2}$ = 80 \\textbf{N} acts at distance \\textbf{d} = 1.12 \\textbf{m} from the left end of the rod and the direction of the force makes $\\mathbf{\\theta_2}$ = $70^\\circ$ with the rod as shown. Acceleration due to gravity is $<0, -10, 0> m/s^2$\n\nWhat is the \\textbf{angular acceleration} of the rod about the pivot point? Note: The moment of inertia of a rod about it's center of mass $I$ = $\\frac{1}{12}ML^2$. You may need to use the parallel axis theorem.",
